OPT-5: SIMD Vectorized Filter — Analysis (LOW PRIORITY FOR JOB)
=================================================================
Date: 2026-07-31

Summary: SIMD filters provide negligible benefit for JOB's top queries.
The bottleneck is probe directory loads, not filter evaluation.

1. Filter Predicates in Top JOB Queries
---------------------------------------
  Query | Filter on cast_info (bottleneck)   | Other filters
  16b   | NONE (joins only)                  | cn.country_code, k.keyword
  8c    | NONE                               | cn.country_code, rt.role
  10c   | ci.note LIKE '%(producer)%'        | t.production_year>1990
  9d    | ci.note IN ('(voice)',...)          | cn.country_code, n.gender
  7c    | NONE                               | an.name LIKE, n.name_pcode_cf
  17f   | NONE                               | k.keyword, n.name LIKE
  19d   | ci.note IN ('(voice)',...)          | t.production_year>2000

  4 of 7 top queries: NO filter on cast_info → SIMD does nothing
  3 of 7: VARCHAR LIKE/IN filters → SIMD can't vectorize (BuildFilterFunctionSIMD
  returns nullptr for VARCHAR at ir_to_llvm.cpp:2995)

2. Numeric Filters Are on Non-Bottleneck Tables
-------------------------------------------------
  t.production_year > 1990/2000: runs on title (2.5M rows), ~7ms
  Even vectorizing this 8x (AVX2): saves ~6ms out of 7ms = ~1ms
  Total impact: <0.5% of query wall time

3. Guard Vectorization Potential
---------------------------------
  Guard range check per row: load key, 2 compares, AND, branch
  36M rows × 5 guards = 180M checks
  Estimated cost: ~53ms (1 cycle/guard at 3.4GHz)
  After 6 workers: ~9ms
  SIMD (8-wide): saves ~8ms → ~4% of 200ms total
  BUT: requires ROF Phase 1 (disabled for TPDE) and rewriting it as vectorized

4. Verified Claims
-------------------
  - CompileQuerySteps uses EmitShortCircuitFilter (scalar): CONFIRMED
  - BuildFilterFunctionSIMD handles INT32/INT64/FLOAT/DOUBLE, rejects VARCHAR: CONFIRMED
  - ROF Phase 1 is scalar (use_simd_ gates ROF enablement, not vectorization): CONFIRMED
  - ROF disabled for TPDE (fast_mode_ != TPDE check at line 9290): CONFIRMED
  - This machine has AVX2 (vec_width=8 for i32): CONFIRMED

5. When SIMD Filters Would Help
---------------------------------
  - Different workload (TPCH/DSB) with numeric predicates on large fact tables
  - Queries where numeric filters on large tables ARE the bottleneck
  - If ROF Phase 1 were enabled for TPDE and vectorized

